# P44 on GtkBackend on macOS (TEST_BACKEND=gtk4): clipped() applied at run time cuts the third cell to its frame.
# Measured 2026-10-16 from p44-macos-gtk4-final-20261016-015923.png (840x1676 = 420x838 pt; 2x halved; origin=frame with the 28 pt title bar). The AppKit file's click at y 153 landed above the button (frame y 170-204; x 16-156) on GTK's taller layout (gtk4-aim-20261016.csv2).
# After this file the label must read third cell: clipped() and cell 3 must be cut to the frame like cell 2, while cell 1 still spills.
# GTK 版 P44:按鈕在 frame y 170-204,AppKit 檔的 y 153 在按鈕上方；改點 (86,187)。
sleep,,,,,,1500000,let P44 lay out its three cells,macos
click,86,187,frame,left,,,"the ""Clip the third cell"" button -- y 153 -> 187 (button centre); cell 3 must go from spilling to cut and the label must read ""third cell: clipped()""",macos
sleep,,,,,,1500000,let the third cell redraw,macos
